.TH FREERAM 1 "August 2026" "freeram 2.1.0"
.SH NAME
freeram \- inspect and optionally drop Linux page caches

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freeram
[\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-silent\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-test\fR]
[\fB\-\-stats\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B freeram
reads Linux memory statistics and can request the kernel to drop page caches by
writing 3 to /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches. Actual cache cleaning requires root;
read-only test and statistics modes do not.

Linux normally manages filesystem cache automatically. Repeated cache clearing
can reduce performance by discarding useful cached data. Use this command only
for a measured operational or troubleshooting need.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the interactive confirmation before a real cache-cleaning run.

.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Suppress normal output. Errors and warnings are still written to standard error.
For cleaning, this option requires --yes.

.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Dry run. Display what would be done without changing kernel caches. Root is not
required.

.TP
.BR \-\-stats
Display current memory information and recent freeram history. Root is not
required.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage help.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information.

.SH OPERATION
For a real cleaning run, freeram reads /proc/meminfo, confirms the request,
checks root privileges, verifies /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches is writable, runs
sync, writes 3 to drop_caches, reads memory statistics again, and records the
observed MemFree change.

The reported freed value is an observation around the operation; memory usage
can change concurrently.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/freeram
Installed command.

.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/freeram.1
Installed manual page.

.TP
.I /var/log/freeram.log
Activity log.

.TP
.I /var/lib/freeram/history
Timestamped before/after history.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Inspect without root:
.B freeram --stats

.TP
Dry run without root:
.B freeram --test

.TP
Interactive cache cleaning:
.B sudo freeram

.TP
Non-interactive cache cleaning:
.B sudo freeram --yes

.TP
Silent automation:
.B sudo freeram --yes --silent

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or an interactive cancellation.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime, environment, privilege, memory-read, or cache-drop error.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line or unsafe non-interactive usage error.

.SH REQUIREMENTS
Linux procfs, Bash 4.0 or newer, awk, sync, and standard core utilities.
Root privileges are required only for actual cache cleaning, installation, and
uninstallation.

.SH AUTHOR
Originally by mrprohack and tamilanmkv.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sync (1)
